  "requiredConformance": [
    "concurrent waiters for one dirty buffer generation share one addressed request and one response wakes them all",
    "concurrent host cursor requests for different buffers and threads remain isolated",
    "a newer dirty generation supersedes the older request without accepting a late response",
    "dirty alternate buffer teardown while GCSBI waits cancels without use-after-free or hang",
    "EOF with an active alternate buffer wakes waiters for every physical screen buffer",
    "matching host response updates only the exact target and generation",
    "stale and malformed twh-cpr-v1 responses are consumed without application-input leakage",
    "foreign OSC 8488 payloads are not claimed by the host RPC",
    "application DSR remains byte-exact through Win32 input mode",
    "request generation and output failures fail closed rather than publishing stale cursor state"
  ]
